WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.701 --> 00:00:03.402
-My next guest is an Emmy-
and Grammy-nominated comedian

00:00:03.402 --> 00:00:06.172
who has a new animated
stand-up special

00:00:06.172 --> 00:00:08.475
called "Tig Notaro: Drawn"

00:00:08.475 --> 00:00:12.311
which premieres July 24th
at 10:00 p.m. on HBO

00:00:12.311 --> 00:00:14.747
and will also be available
on HBO Max.

00:00:14.747 --> 00:00:18.117
Please welcome Tig Notaro!

00:00:18.117 --> 00:00:22.255
-♪ It's Tig Notaro,
the girl is incredible ♪

00:00:22.255 --> 00:00:26.392
♪ She's animated
in a TV show called "Drawn" ♪

00:00:26.392 --> 00:00:30.363
♪ It's Tig Notaro
changing up her tune ♪

00:00:30.363 --> 00:00:34.567
♪ Might not recognize her
'cause now she's a cartoon ♪

00:00:34.567 --> 00:00:37.604
♪ Yeah ♪
-It's a very big move.

00:00:37.604 --> 00:00:41.508
-Tig Notaro.
That's Tig Notaro right there.

00:00:41.508 --> 00:00:44.310
-How come --
How come you didn't have me on

00:00:44.310 --> 00:00:46.379
to do that game?

00:00:46.379 --> 00:00:47.914
[ Laughter ]

00:00:47.914 --> 00:00:50.884
-"The Mimic"? I didn't know
that you could do, uh, sounds.

00:00:50.884 --> 00:00:53.052
-Yeah, well, I'm known for them.

00:00:53.052 --> 00:00:54.720
[ Laughter ]

00:00:54.720 --> 00:00:56.422
-I didn't know
that you were known for them.

00:00:56.422 --> 00:00:57.957
There's other things
that I think you were known for,

00:00:57.957 --> 00:01:00.326
but sounds -- you doing --
mimicking sounds?

00:01:00.326 --> 00:01:01.360
-Yes.

00:01:01.360 --> 00:01:03.296
For instance,

00:01:03.296 --> 00:01:06.799
this is a spring.

00:01:06.799 --> 00:01:08.334
Doi-oi-oi-oi-oi-oing.

00:01:08.334 --> 00:01:10.169
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:10.169 --> 00:01:12.004 line:0%
♪♪

00:01:12.004 --> 00:01:14.140
[ Bell dings ]

00:01:14.140 --> 00:01:15.875
[ Applause ]

00:01:15.875 --> 00:01:18.044
The next one
is a curtain opening.

00:01:18.044 --> 00:01:20.145
-[ Laughing ] Okay.

00:01:20.145 --> 00:01:22.615
-[ Sniffing sharply ]

00:01:22.615 --> 00:01:23.716
[ Laughter ]

00:01:23.716 --> 00:01:24.750
[ Bell dings ]

00:01:24.750 --> 00:01:26.852 line:0%
♪♪

00:01:26.852 --> 00:01:29.455
-[ Laughing ]

00:01:29.455 --> 00:01:30.489
That's really good.

00:01:30.489 --> 00:01:31.557
-Thank you.
-That's really well done.

00:01:31.557 --> 00:01:32.658
I love that one. Yeah.

00:01:32.658 --> 00:01:35.194
-Well, prepare yourself,
because...

00:01:35.194 --> 00:01:36.862
[ Laughter ]

00:01:36.862 --> 00:01:40.400
...this is a clown horn.

00:01:40.400 --> 00:01:41.801
[ Honks, wheezes ]

00:01:41.801 --> 00:01:43.202
[ Laughter ]

00:01:43.202 --> 00:01:45.638
[ Imitating horn honking ]

00:01:45.638 --> 00:01:48.041
[ Bell dings ]
-Whoa, why didn't we do that?

00:01:48.041 --> 00:01:50.209
We should have had Tig
play the game.

00:01:50.209 --> 00:01:53.345
You could have played against
Tom Hiddleston and crushed him.

00:01:53.345 --> 00:01:54.380
[ Imitates horn honk ]

00:01:54.380 --> 00:01:56.682
[ Laughter ]

00:01:56.682 --> 00:01:58.817
[ Imitating horn honking ]
-I got you. I heard you, yeah,

00:01:58.817 --> 00:01:59.986
I -- Thank you.

00:01:59.986 --> 00:02:01.220
[ Laughter ]

00:02:01.220 --> 00:02:04.289
You -- Tig,
your kids just turned 5.

00:02:04.289 --> 00:02:05.892
-They did. They turned 5.

00:02:05.892 --> 00:02:08.427
-Yeah, and you posted
this revelation

00:02:08.427 --> 00:02:10.463
that they had
about getting older.

00:02:10.463 --> 00:02:13.332
-Mm-hmm.
-And I thought it was touching.

00:02:13.332 --> 00:02:15.034
I thought it was nice.

00:02:15.034 --> 00:02:18.104
-Well, yeah,
they were in preschool.

00:02:18.104 --> 00:02:20.373
You know, when the pandemic
started, they were 3.

00:02:20.373 --> 00:02:22.708
We pulled them out
and kept them home.

00:02:22.708 --> 00:02:26.145
And then they were
returning to a new school

00:02:26.145 --> 00:02:27.913
that was starting
with summer school

00:02:27.913 --> 00:02:30.616
that was going to just
turn into junior kindergarten.

00:02:30.616 --> 00:02:35.455
And they are 5 now.

00:02:35.455 --> 00:02:38.391
And when they saw
their old backpacks hanging,

00:02:38.391 --> 00:02:44.530
they said, "Uh, we are not
bringing our old backpacks.

00:02:44.530 --> 00:02:47.600
Those are for babies."

00:02:47.600 --> 00:02:50.135
-I'm so sad. I mean,
here's the old backpack.

00:02:50.135 --> 00:02:52.138
-Yeah. They were like, "No way.

00:02:52.138 --> 00:02:54.473
We are big boys now.

00:02:54.473 --> 00:02:57.309
We're not bringing
our old backpacks."

00:02:57.309 --> 00:02:59.645
-So you got them new backpacks.

00:02:59.645 --> 00:03:03.048
-Well, they had these,
but they dug them out,

00:03:03.048 --> 00:03:06.852
because they realized
they were the big boy backpacks,

00:03:06.852 --> 00:03:10.023
and so they wanted
to start bringing those now.

00:03:10.023 --> 00:03:11.157
-Yeah.

00:03:11.157 --> 00:03:14.360
[ Laughter ]

00:03:14.360 --> 00:03:19.198
-So, it's goodbye, childhood.

00:03:19.198 --> 00:03:21.701
[ Laughter ]

00:03:21.701 --> 00:03:23.236
Hello, real world.

00:03:23.236 --> 00:03:25.304
[ Laughter ]

00:03:25.304 --> 00:03:27.807
-That's was the cutest --
Come on.

00:03:27.807 --> 00:03:30.142
That's the best thing ever.

00:03:30.142 --> 00:03:32.545
-And if you could go in closer,

00:03:32.545 --> 00:03:35.614
it has little feet dangling

00:03:35.614 --> 00:03:38.217
for when they get to the office,
you know?

00:03:38.217 --> 00:03:39.619
-Absolutely, right?

00:03:39.619 --> 00:03:42.121
I thought that was so cute.

00:03:42.121 --> 00:03:45.625
I want to talk about
"Tig Notaro: Drawn."

00:03:45.625 --> 00:03:47.460
-Yeah.
-This is your stand-up special,

00:03:47.460 --> 00:03:48.961
but the whole thing is animated.

00:03:48.961 --> 00:03:52.264
-Yeah, it's fully animated
and --

00:03:52.264 --> 00:03:54.199
-Where'd you get
the idea for this?

00:03:54.199 --> 00:03:57.503
-Well, it's been around,
animating stand-up.

00:03:57.503 --> 00:04:00.072
In fact, you know,
there's TV shows,

00:04:00.072 --> 00:04:04.410
and other comedians have used it
in their specials, and my --

00:04:04.410 --> 00:04:07.079
-I haven't seen
a full special, though.

00:04:07.079 --> 00:04:09.882
-No, I think
not start to finish.

00:04:09.882 --> 00:04:14.754
There's no actual, live Tig
in the special.

00:04:14.754 --> 00:04:16.122
-It is fantastic,

00:04:16.122 --> 00:04:18.991
'cause there's a bunch
of different Tigs in this.

00:04:18.991 --> 00:04:21.226
There's different
versions of you.

00:04:21.226 --> 00:04:24.363
-Yeah. It's really interesting
when people draw you,

00:04:24.363 --> 00:04:28.133
because it's flattering,
but it's also

00:04:28.133 --> 00:04:30.069
like, "Oh.

00:04:30.069 --> 00:04:32.138
That's how you see me."

00:04:32.138 --> 00:04:33.706
[ Laughter ]

00:04:33.706 --> 00:04:37.476
Or, "Am I that unattractive?"

00:04:37.476 --> 00:04:39.545
-No, stop. Come on.
-You know?

00:04:39.545 --> 00:04:41.714
-Stop it.
-I mean, it's just a funny thing

00:04:41.714 --> 00:04:44.217
when you see yourself.
-Yeah.

00:04:44.217 --> 00:04:47.153
-Because it truly is flattering.

00:04:47.153 --> 00:04:49.488
-This is "Tig Notaro: Drawn."

00:04:49.488 --> 00:04:50.857
Take a look at this.

00:04:50.857 --> 00:04:54.093
-And there was this woman
that annoyed me to no end.

00:04:54.093 --> 00:04:58.097
And when I was cleaning up,
sweeping, she was talking to me,

00:04:58.097 --> 00:05:00.999
and I rarely paid attention
to what she said.

00:05:00.999 --> 00:05:02.735
And this was so long ago.

00:05:02.735 --> 00:05:06.072
And she was, like, going on and
on about dinosaurs

00:05:06.072 --> 00:05:08.207
and how they were, you know,
eating people.

00:05:08.207 --> 00:05:10.475
And I was like, "Wait, what?

00:05:10.475 --> 00:05:13.646
Why are we just
standing here --"

00:05:13.646 --> 00:05:16.448
And she's like, "Yeah,
like, scientists, you know,

00:05:16.448 --> 00:05:20.886
took an insect
and took the blood and --"

00:05:20.886 --> 00:05:22.654
And I was like,
"And they're just running around

00:05:22.654 --> 00:05:24.323
eating people."
She's like, "Yes,

00:05:24.323 --> 00:05:26.859
I can't believe
you haven't heard about this."

00:05:26.859 --> 00:05:29.462
Had no idea
it was "Jurassic Park."

00:05:29.462 --> 00:05:30.963
[ Laughter ]

00:05:30.963 --> 00:05:34.933
-Tig Notaro.
Check out "Tig Notaro: Drawn"

00:05:34.933 --> 00:05:40.239
July 24th at 10:00 p.m. on HBO
and streaming on HBO Max.

